    {
      "id": "0011",
      "front": "Use integration by parts to find a reduction formula for $I_n = \\int x^n e^x\\,dx$, and hence evaluate $I_3$.",
      "back": "$I_n = x^n e^x - nI_{n-1}$, and $I_3 = e^x(x^3 - 3x^2 + 6x - 6) + c$.",
      "answerType": "EXPRESSION",
      "keyPoints": [
        {
          "text": "I_n = x^n e^x - n I_(n-1)",
          "synonyms": [
            "differentiate x^n and integrate e^x"
          ],
          "mustInclude": true
        },
        {
          "text": "I_0 = e^x + c",
          "synonyms": [
            "the base of the reduction"
          ],
          "mustInclude": true
        },
        {
          "text": "e^x(x^3 - 3x^2 + 6x - 6) + c",
          "synonyms": [
            "apply the formula three times"
          ],
          "mustInclude": true
        }
      ],
      "mcq": {
        "correct": "$I_n = x^ne^x - nI_{n-1}$; $I_3 = e^x(x^3 - 3x^2 + 6x - 6) + c$",
        "distractors": [
          "$I_n = x^ne^x + nI_{n-1}$; $I_3 = e^x(x^3 + 3x^2 + 6x + 6) + c$",
          "$I_n = nx^{n-1}e^x - I_{n-1}$; $I_3 = e^x(x^3 - 3x^2 + 6x - 6) + c$",
          "$I_n = x^ne^x - I_{n-1}$; $I_3 = e^x(x^3 - x^2 + x - 1) + c$"
        ]
      },
      "explanation": "With $u = x^n$ and $\\frac{dv}{dx} = e^x$, $I_n = x^ne^x - n\\int x^{n-1}e^x\\,dx = x^ne^x - nI_{n-1}$. Since $I_0 = e^x$, $I_1 = e^x(x - 1)$, $I_2 = e^x(x^2 - 2x + 2)$ and $I_3 = e^x(x^3 - 3x^2 + 6x - 6)$. The coefficients 1, 3, 6 are the factorials building up, which is a useful check on the arithmetic.",
      "reviewStatus": "AI_UNREVIEWED",
